# librapidarchive (rapidgzip) vendored for gpukallisto

Pinned commit: `1221a30bb548b305a69e5715f2bc348ba37ac243`

Upstream: https://github.com/mxmlnkn/librapidarchive

Used for multithreaded CPU gzip decompression via `rapidgzip::ParallelGzipReader`
when input FASTQ files are regular gzip (not BGZF).

This is a **trimmed vendored copy**: C++ library sources and bundled dependencies
only (no python bindings, benchmark results, tests, or tools).

Bundled deps under `src/external/`: zlib-ng, rpmalloc, isa-l (igzip+crc), cxxopts.

## Refreshing (requires network)

```bash
./scripts/vendor_librapidarchive.sh   # clone, vendor deps, trim
```

## Building without rapidgzip

`USE_RAPIDGZIP` defaults to ON. If the tree is missing or incomplete, CMake falls
back to single-threaded zlib gzip:

```bash
cmake -DUSE_RAPIDGZIP=OFF ..
```

